  "notes": "Vitra Eames Plastic Armchair RE RAR, the rocking armchair (design Charles & Ray Eames, 1950), configured as in the user's picture: shell ice grey, seat cushion in a pale blue-grey, wire base powder-coated basic dark, runners in dark stained maple. W 62.5 × D 69 × H 67 cm, seat height 33 cm, arms about 58 cm, from Vitra's dimension drawing. model.glb is generated by `npx tsx tools/models/armchair-eames-rar.ts` from its own geometry: the one-piece moulded armchair shell (arms sweeping up from the seat into the back, which rises above them; rolled rim), traced from the to-scale drawing of the rocker on dimensions.com, then shortened and set on the base as in Vitra's photos (side and front three-quarter views, cameras fitted on the runners): the shell is about 56 cm deep and stands well inside the 69 cm runners, the top of its back about 8 cm in front of the runners' back ends; the runners are 42.4 cm apart. The collision parts follow the runners, the base and the shell in four layers. The clearance zone is legroom in front and room behind for rocking."
